//! BigSky Cloud's first pass through its tank, pulse for pulse — the taps
//! of [`super::cloud_ring::CloudRing`]. Generated, do not edit by hand.
//!
//! Read off the Strymon BigSky plug-in (signal-analyzer `bigsky_match`,
//! `pulses.py`) with Cloud at Diffusion −10 (every allpass a pure delay),
//! MOD 0, Tone 127, Low End +10, Pre-Delay 0 and Decay 1000 — where the
//! loop returns at −80 dB, so what comes out is one pass and nothing else.
//! 454 pulses above 0.003 over 3 s; together they carry the response's
//! energy to within 0.3 dB in every 250 ms window. Their envelope falls
//! ~13 dB/s: BigSky's 4.5 s decay floor is the length of this one pass,
//! not a decay process.
//!
